Use callback clone where GNU tar requires fork-like child setup

wasm Linux has no fork syscall.  Its callback clone without CLONE_VM gives a
single-threaded caller's child a private copy of memory and descriptors with
fork-like process semantics, while starting at an explicit function on a fresh
stack.  Restructure tar's fork sites around that interface without changing the
compressor/reblocking topology, child-only TAR_* environment setup, privilege
restoration, status propagation, or remote-rsh protocol.

The kernel rejects a non-CLONE_VM snapshot when another task shares the address
space.  GNU tar creates no threads, so these process-creation sites satisfy that
constraint.  Keep a native fork fallback so the patched source remains usable
outside wasm builds.

